<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">kenshi</ansi>

The Kenshi is the neutral elite of the Ronin: the swordsman who fights on
alone. Every fallen ally sharpens its blade, it cannot be knocked down when it
is the last one standing, and Zanshin follows every kill.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Last stand         it cannot be knocked down while it is the last of its
                        company standing
  35 Grim tally         +20% damage for each fallen ally
  40 Cold edge          +4 Attack
  45 Lone wolf          +6 Evasion
  50 Deeper tally       +25% damage for each fallen ally
  55 Death's eye        +5% critical chance
  60 Endless stillness  Zanshin works every time it fells a foe, not once a
                        round

It needs the Ronin first (<ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] kenshi confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Samurai talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Razor's Edge (+5% critical chance
on every blow), Quick Hands (starts a battle with 15 points on its action
meter), Shadow Footing (+5 Evasion). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
